  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(427.56pt, 169.8pt, "1 ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.92pt, 194.76pt, "1. College of Water Resources and Architectural Engineering, Northwest A&F University, Yangling, China ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 210.36pt, "2. College of Civil Engineering and Architecture, Zhejiang University, Hangzhou, China ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(210pt, 232.8pt, "Corresponding author: zh.xiong@nwsuaf.edu.cn ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.04pt, 252.96pt, "ABSTRACT: ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.92pt, 252.72pt, "Given the widespread application of high-performance materials in cyclic ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 272.76pt, "loaded infrastructure, a thorough understanding of the fracture and high-cycle fatigue behavior ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 292.68pt, "of high-performance materials is of critical importance. However, these behaviors ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 312.72pt, "predominantly rely on experimental methods, which are often costly, time-consuming and ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 332.76pt, "limited in generalizability. To address these issues, this paper proposes the constitution and ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 352.68pt, "high-cycle fatigue of Ultra-High Performance Concrete (UHPC) and High Strength Steel (HSS) ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 372.72pt, "within the Phase-Field Cohesive Zone Model (PF-CZM) framework. A generic stress-based ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 392.76pt, "failure criterion for UHPC is derived from the biaxial tensile test results to calculate crack ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 412.68pt, "driving force. Furthermore, a fatigue degradation function and an acceleration algorithm are ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 432.72pt, "integrated into the PF-CZM framework to enable efficient high-cycle fatigue simulations. In ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 452.76pt, "the acceleration algorithm, the envelope load is used to approximate the real cyclic load to avoid ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 472.68pt, "the simulation of each cycle, and the three-stage fatigue process is simulated through adjusting ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 492.72pt, "the cyclic increment adaptively. The proposed model successfully captures mixed-mode ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 512.76pt, "fracture and high-cycle fatigue behavior of UHPC and HSS, with validation provided through ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 532.68pt, "relevant experimental comparisons. ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.04pt, 552.96pt, "Keywords: ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(153.6pt, 552.72pt, "high performance material; Phase-field model; accelerated algorithm; fatigue; ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 572.76pt, "high cycle; fracture. ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 15.001pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.92pt, 605.28pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(94.92pt, 631.68pt, "High performance materials, such as High Strength Steel (HSS) and Ultra-High ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 651.72pt, "Performance Concrete (UHPC) are integral to demanding applications in civil and mechanical ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 671.76pt, "engineering due to their superior mechanical properties [1-4].")
  #line-at(372.96pt, 671.76pt, "In structures like wind turbines ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 691.68pt, "and bridges, they are routinely subjected to cyclic loading, where fracture and fatigue ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 711.72pt, "phenomena can lead to catastrophic failures [5-6]. However, modeling the fracture and fatigue ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 731.76pt, "behavior of these materials remains a significant challenge, especially for High Cycle Fatigue ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 751.68pt, "(HCF) scenarios involving millions of load cycles, which are often computationally prohibitive ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.92pt, 101.52pt, "to simulate. For the above issues, Phase-Field Cohesive Zone Model (PF-CZM) is a promising ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 121.44pt, "solution. ")
  #line-at(94.92pt, 141.48pt, "Phase Field Models (PFM) originated from the linearly elastic variational principle, which ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 161.52pt, "is a powerful framework for simulating complex crack. It avoids pre-defining the crack path in ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 181.44pt, "Griffith’s energy theory, more importantly it enables predictions of the crack nucleation, ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 201.48pt, "propagation and branching [7-8]. Based on PFM, the PF-CZM was introduced by Wu to better ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 221.52pt, "model both brittle and quasi-brittle fracture [9]. This is achieved by incorporating a ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 241.44pt, "parameterized crack geometry function and an energy degradation function, which respectively ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 261.48pt, "characterize the distribution of phase field crack and the strain energy dissipation during failure. ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 281.52pt, "Consequently, PF-CZM accurately predicts multiple softening curves and mitigates the mesh ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 301.44pt, "sensitivity associated with the length-scale parameter in traditional PFM, proving its utility in ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 321.48pt, "the fracture analysis of various materials [10-13]. ")
  #line-at(94.92pt, 341.52pt, "To apply the PFM to fatigue analysis, two approaches are commonly employed: 1) ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 361.44pt, "introducing fatigue degradation functions related to historical variables to reduce fracture ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 381.48pt, "toughness [14-15], 2) adding an additional energy term to explain irreversible fatigue damage, ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.92pt, 401.52pt, "i.e.")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.56pt, 401.52pt, ", considering the fatigue mechanism occurring in the material as an additional contribution ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 421.44pt, "to the driving force [16-17]. In the analysis of high cycle fatigue, both of the above approaches ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 441.48pt, "are computationally intensive due to the presence of a large number of load cycles. To overcome ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 461.52pt, "this bottleneck, several fatigue acceleration algorithms for brittle fracture in PFM have been ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 481.44pt, "developed, including adaptive cyclic increment adjustment algorithm [18-20], cycle jump ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 501.48pt, "method [21-22] and adaptive meshing method [23-24]. These methods reduce computation time ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 521.52pt, "by adjusting the cyclic increment, jumping cycles and reducing the number of meshes, ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 541.44pt, "respectively. ")
  #line-at(94.92pt, 561.48pt, "Despite these advances, significant research gaps persist for specific high-performance ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 581.52pt, "materials. For fracture and fatigue of Ultra-High Performance Concrete (UHPC), experimental ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 601.44pt, "studies have explored the effects of aggregate size, steel fiber volume fractions etc. [25-")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 621.48pt, "27], leading to empirical fatigue life predictions [28]. However, numerical simulations for ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 641.52pt, "fatigue of UHPC are scarce, often limited to low-cycle fatigue [29] or are unable to reproduce ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 661.44pt, "the complete three-stage crack propagation process [30]. Similarly, for High Strength Steel ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 681.48pt, "(HSS), research has focused on experimental characterization of its ductile-to-brittle transition ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 701.52pt, "at low temperatures [31-33], with microstructural analyses explaining the underlying ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 721.44pt, "mechanisms [34-35]. The brittle fracture of large-scale screws made of HSS at low temperatures ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 741.48pt, "was also studied [36]. Yet, robust numerical models capable of predicting the low-temperature ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 761.52pt, "fracture behavior are notably absent. ")
]

