#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 345pt), 147pt, 637pt))[
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(94.92pt, 101.52pt, "In general, most of the research on the fracture and fatigue performance of typical high ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 121.44pt, "performance materials are based on experiments, which are often costly, time-consuming and ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 141.48pt, "limited in generalizability. This paper aims to bridge these gaps by developing a comprehensive ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 161.52pt, "and computationally efficient framework for modeling fracture and HCF in high-performance ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 181.44pt, "materials. We extend the PF-CZM to HCF analysis by integrating a fatigue degradation function ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 201.48pt, "with an acceleration algorithm. Specifically, for UHPC, we propose a new constitutive model ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 221.52pt, "and a generic stress-based failure criterion, calibrated against uniaxial and biaxial test data. ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 241.44pt, "Within this unified framework, mode-I and mixed-mode fracture simulation of UHPC and HSS ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 261.48pt, "at low temperature are achieved, and further investigation is conducted on the high cycle mode-")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 281.52pt, "I and mixed-mode fatigue of UHPC. The accuracy of the proposed model is verified through ")
  #line-at(70.92pt, 301.44pt, "relevant tests. ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 15.001pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
