// arXiv source page 31
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-31.png", width: 7.5pt), 104.5pt, 308pt))[
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(73.68pt, 101.52pt, "angle decreases as demonstrated in Fig. 18 (b). As the loading angle decreases, shear stress on ")
  #line-at(73.68pt, 121.44pt, "the crack surface increases while normal stress decreases. Consequently, crack propagation ")
  #line-at(73.68pt, 141.48pt, "becomes shear-dominated, progressing toward a horizontal (pure-shear) orientation. The PF-")
  #line-at(73.68pt, 161.52pt, "CZM predictions accurately capture this transition. ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 15.001pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(73.68pt, 201.84pt, "5. Conclusions ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(97.68pt, 236.04pt, "In this study, a Phase-Field Cohesive Zone Model (PF-CZM) is employed to model the ")
  #line-at(73.68pt, 256.08pt, "fracture and high-cycle fatigue behavior of Ultra-High Performance Concrete (UHPC) and ")
  #line-at(73.68pt, 276.12pt, "High Strength Steel (HSS), incorporating a fatigue degradation function and an acceleration ")
  #line-at(73.68pt, 296.04pt, "algorithm. The main conclusions are as follows: ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 316.08pt, "The energy degradation function applicable to UHPC is analyzed based on the ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 336.12pt, "uniaxial tensile test results of UHPC. The constitutive model of UHPC in the PF-")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 356.04pt, "CZM framework is established, achieving effective simulation of Ⅰ-mode fracture ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 376.08pt, "of UHPC. ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 396.12pt, "A generic stress-based failure criterion for UHPC, ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(388.32pt, 396.12pt, "i.e.")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(402.96pt, 396.12pt, ", the hyperbolic biaxial ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 416.04pt, "strength envelope, is derived. With this criterion, it opens up the precise calculation ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 436.08pt, "of the crack driving force and effective simulation of mixed-mode fracture of ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 456.12pt, "UHPC. ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 476.04pt, "A fatigue degradation function and an acceleration algorithm are integrated into PF-")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 496.08pt, "CZM, and the fatigue damage accumulation parameter is calibrated through test ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 516.12pt, "results, enabling effective simulation of mode-I and mixed-mode high cycle fatigue ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 536.04pt, "of UHPC. ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 556.08pt, "The PF-CZM framework is successfully extended to HSS. Precise reproducing of ")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 576.12pt, "mode-I and mixed-mode fracture of HSS at low temperatures is achieved using PF-")
  #line-at(125.76pt, 596.04pt, "CZM. ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 15.001pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
